### Research memory → `experiments/` (LEDGER + ROADMAP + INBOX + REPORTs)

This project tracks experiments with the `experiment-knowledge-harness`
skill (sibling of `project-knowledge-harness`; engineering chores still go
to `TODO.md`, debugging traps to `pitfalls/`).

**Before designing or running ANY experiment**: grep
[`experiments/LEDGER.md`](experiments/LEDGER.md) and the map + index in
[`experiments/README.md`](experiments/README.md). The direction may
already be settled — or already a documented dead end whose assumptions
haven't changed. Cite findings as `F-xxx` instead of re-deriving them.

Core loop (scripts live in the skill folder, run with `python3`):

1. **Queue an idea** — add to [`experiments/ROADMAP.md`](experiments/ROADMAP.md)
   with mandatory `payoff:` (with units) and `cat:`
   (`research`/`engineering`/`data`/`tooling`/`infra`), plus
   `depends-on: F-xxx` when its priority assumes a finding. Research sparks
   that can't be priced yet go to [`experiments/INBOX.md`](experiments/INBOX.md)
   (humans append free-text bullets there directly). When asked to **sweep
   the experiments inbox**: run `scripts/sweep-inbox.py`, ask the user the
   listed open judgments per entry (never invent a `payoff:`), then
   `--formalize N` each resolved entry into its lane.
2. **Start an experiment** — `scripts/new-experiment.py --title ... --question ...
   --axis ... --baseline ...` allocates `#NNN`, scaffolds
   `experiments/<NNN>-<slug>/REPORT.md`. Fill **Pre-registration**
   (hypothesis, success criteria, decision rule) *before running*; if the
   decision rule's branches are identical, don't run it.
3. **While running** — append dated bullets to the REPORT `## Log`; add
   results rows as they land. One ablation axis per experiment, vs the
   named `baseline:`; tables always state their `spec:` (cost model / fee /
   eval-window version) and never mix specs.
4. **Conclude (success OR failure)** — write `## Conclusion` (negative
   results need the dead-end clause: "do not retry unless X changes"),
   paste the `scripts/snapshot-provenance.py` block, distill 1–5 findings
   via `scripts/log-finding.py`, then `scripts/render-index.py` and move
   the ROADMAP item to `## Done`.
5. **On overturned findings** — `log-finding.py --overturns F-xxx` moves the
   old finding to the graveyard; immediately run `scripts/retriage.py` and
   re-sort the flagged ROADMAP items with the user.

Run `scripts/render-index.py --validate-only` after hand-editing any
surface; the map + index bodies in `experiments/README.md` are generated
(experiments coloured by status, `baseline:`/`refs:`/`depends-on:` edges,
queued ROADMAP items) — never edit the sentinel blocks manually.
